# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Controller input for Killzone (SCES-52004): the same way through the menus
# into the first level of the campaign as level1.pad, and then the level
# played otherwise: other directions, other looks, more fire. For training
# profile-guided optimization (scripts\windows\build.ps1 -Pgo), so that the
# run that is timed, level1.pad, is not the run the compiler was taught by.
# Run it for 17,500 frames.
#
# This file holds button presses, written for PS2Native's tests. Nothing in
# it comes from the game.
#
# frame  input  frames held

# "No memory card (PS2) found ... Do you want to start the game?": Continue.
1900    cross     4
# The intro film: skip it. The title screen follows.
2300    cross     4
# The title screen: to the main menu (Options, Game, Extras).
2500    start     4
# Game, then Campaign. The game looks for a memory card and asks for a profile.
2900    cross     4
3300    cross     4

# "Create profile": edit the profile name. The game's keyboard takes a letter
# when a direction is held and a button pressed meanwhile: three letters.
3700    cross     4
3800    up        60
3830    cross     4
3900    l_up      60
3930    cross     4
4000    l_left    60
4030    cross     4
# With no direction held, Cross is "enter": the name is done.
4200    cross     4
# Down to "Create profile", and create it.
4300    down      30
4450    cross     4
# "Do you want to save this profile to the memory card?": No.
4700    triangle  4

# Select level (the first), difficulty (Normal), character (the first).
5000    cross     4
5300    cross     4
5600    cross     4
# The level's opening scene: skip it. The level loads until about frame 6,600.
5900    cross     4

# In the level, otherwise than level1.pad plays it.
6700    l_left    200
6800    r1        120
7000    r_left    60
7100    l_up      400
7300    r1        80
7400    l_right   150
7600    r_up      40
7700    r1        150
7900    l_down    100
8000    square    4
8100    l_up      500
8300    r_right   80
8500    r1        200
8800    l_left    300
9000    r1        100
9200    l_up      700
9500    r_left    40
9700    r1        150
10000   l_right   400
10200   r1        120
10500   l_up      800
10800   r_down    20
11000   r1        200
11400   l_left    300
11700   r1        150
12000   l_up      900
12400   r_right   60
12600   r1        200
13000   l_up      900
13400   r1        150
14000   l_right   300
14300   r1        200

# Whatever has happened by now: Retry, should "Failed" be up, and play on.
15200   cross     4
15500   triangle  4
16600   l_up      300
16800   r1        60
17100   r_left    60
17200   r1        60
